#edb/ref 17592186249191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250005 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c3dd683c-9379-5f34-9cdb-095ffd9b03f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250172 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186249899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250172 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114046" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250172 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250172 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{9}{81+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250172 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e7b39f3-407b-599d-a487-d698e967777b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250172 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{81+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{9}{81\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/81)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/81}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/9)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\n The only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{9})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{9}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{9}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=9\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{81+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/9)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (9\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318118 #edb/ref 1080 "\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318118 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318118 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a18383d3-63cd-5639-931d-a7a1c504ecad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318876 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186318118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318876 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186527772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318876 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318876 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318876 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186527772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318876 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d4db02f7-5977-595a-8560-ebd6520e3bc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319994 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319994 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319994 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c4d6374a-a8f4-5012-ba14-79979bb09a1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320599 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186319994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320599 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186537260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320599 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320599 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320599 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186537260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320599 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d0e46496-0573-5f7f-b6a6-15d10b4e8306" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320917 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320917 #edb/ref 1069 "q-351834" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320917 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320917 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-75{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320917 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "88256796-f1d7-5511-b30e-ef033cdfdfae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320917 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-75{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3\\cdot (1-25{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(5x)}^{2}.$   \n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-0.2$ | $0.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-75{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\,\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330078 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{9})+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330078 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330078 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0edb1c73-87ee-58c2-a730-43e7f693d596" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330187 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)}{6}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330187 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330187 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1afb9d8c-3f67-5